# Belt-and-suspenders exclusion for the published npm tarball.
#
# `files` in package.json is an ALLOWLIST (dist + LICENSE + NOTICE +
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md + README.md) and is the primary control — npm only
# packs what `files` lists. This `.npmignore` is defense-in-depth: even if
# `files` is ever loosened, none of the paths below can leak into the
# tarball. In particular, tests/fixtures/ contains fabricated key-shaped
# literals (secrets-detector fixtures) that must never ship (T-08-05).
tests/
src/
.planning/
docs/
*.test.*
tsconfig.json
vitest.config.ts
tsup.config.ts
.github/
